      "en": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(As we leave the serenity of the Shabbos and transition into the dangers of the day-to-day workweek, we proclaim—to ourselves—that:) יֹשֵׁב בְּסֵתֶר—I put my complete trust in Hashem that He will shelter and protect me from all my enemies and all troubles. There is no need to fear the terror of the night (enemies and difficulties that I do not even know about) or be afraid of the \"arrows\" of the day (dangers and difficulties that I am aware of). For Hashem will instruct His angels to protect me wherever I go. (Hashem responds to this declaration of trust in Him:) \"Since he desires (and is doing his best) to be close to Me, I will rescue him. When he calls out to Me, I will answer him. עִמּוֹ אָנֹכִי בְּצָרָה—I will be with him in his difficulty and suffering, and I will rescue him. I will grant him a long life and will show him My salvation!\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "וְאַתָּה קָדוֹשׁ—We realize that You, Hashem, are completely beyond our comprehension, yet we sing Your praises, just as the angels in Heaven proclaim:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ—The sanctity of Hashem can be felt in ALL worlds, from the very highest world of angels down to the very lowest world, our material world; מָלֹא—His Presence can be felt everywhere. And as the Serafim (the highest levels of angels) proclaim: בָּרוּךְ כְּבוֹד יְהֹוָה—The essence of Hashem is completely beyond us (even the highest angels); it is מִמְּקוֹמוֹ—from His place (up there, it all makes sense!)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 18
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיִשְׂרָאֵל אֲבוֹתֵינוּ—(As we go out and face the world we ask:) Hashem Who took care of our ancestors, please direct our hearts to Your service and have mercy on us when we make mistakes, for You, Hashem, are forgiving and are kind to all who call to You. Shower us with Your blessings and save us from difficulties. Happy is the person who places their trust in You!"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 2
        }
      ],
      "_legacySource": null
    },
